// A `pub use` is where a module boundary is crossed, so it is where crossing
// it is checked. It has to resolve the module in the file that wrote it: this
// file imported `alpha`, so `alpha.pick` is alpha's, and alpha's is private.
//
// Scanning the whole module for a binding of that name found the one another
// file wrote -- a different module, under the same name -- and re-exported
// something from it. The visibility check then asked about the wrong module
// and found nothing to object to.
import alpha

pub use alpha.pick

fn main() -> UInt8 {
    pick() + helper()
}
